  "text": "\r\n\t\t Government | Newmarket, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     Government   \t\t\t \n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Services   \t\t\t \n     How Do I...   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \nHome \nGovernment \r\nGovernment\t\t \r\n9 \n1 \n1 \n2 \t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\nAccess easily searchable meeting agendas and minutes for various boards, commissions, and committees. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t About Newmarket \r\nThe ideal combination of location, skilled and available work force, and the friendliness and safety of a small town. Encourage the creativity and growth of your firm by locating it in an area with available land and buildings, and a responsive pro-business environment where your staff will enjoy the New Hampshire way of life.  \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Boards & Commissions \r\nDiscover the boards and commissions that drive your local government. Find agendas, member information, and other meeting details. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Town Council \r\nThe Town of Newmarket operates under the Town Council form of government, in accordance with the Town Charter adopted 1991. Registered voters elect Councilors to represent them for a term of three years, and each year three seats are open for re-election. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Watch Meetings \r\nAccess live Meetings and On-Demand Videos to watch various board and committee meetings. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Town Meeting 2027 \r\nThis page will have all the information for the Town Meeting and links to the School District Meeting. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Election Information \r\nElection Information\r\nFind dates, deadlines, and details for upcoming local, state, and federal elections, including polling locations, hours, and absentee ballot procedures.\r\nSupervisors of the Checklist Meetings\r\nView the schedule of meetings held by the Supervisors of the Checklist, where residents can register to vote, update their voter registration information, or verify their status on the town's voter checklist.\r\nState of New Hampshire Primary Election\r\nAccess official information from the State of New Hampshire regarding the Primary Election, including key dates, candidate filings, and ballot information.\r\nState of NH Voter Information Lookup\r\nUse this tool provided by the New Hampshire Secretary of State's office to verify your voter registration status, find your polling place, and view sample ballots for upcoming elections. \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t About Newmarket \r\n\t\t\t\t Business \r\n\t\t\t\t Education \r\n\t\t\t\t Location \r\n\t\t\t\t Town Statistics \r\n\t\t\t\t Election Information \r\n\t\t\t Boards & Commissions \r\n\t\t\t\t Riverfront Advisory Committee \r\n\t\t\t\t (LRAC) Lamprey River Advisory Committee Website \r\n\t\t\t\t Newmarket Design Charrette Report \r\n\t\t\t\t Arts, Culture, & Tourism Commission \r\n\t\t\t\t Events \r\n\t\t\t\t Project Photos \r\n\t\t\t\t Willey House Main Street Park \r\n\t\t\t\t Elm Street Mural Revitalization \r\n\t\t\t\t Mural Photos \r\n\t\t\t\t Budget Committee \r\n\t\t\t\t Capital Improvement Program (CIP) Committee \r\n\t\t\t\t Cemetery Trustees \r\n\t\t\t\t Charter Commission \r\n\t\t\t\t Conservation Commission \r\n\t\t\t\t Agendas & Packets \r\n\t\t\t\t Annual Reports \r\n\t\t\t\t Conservation Areas & Parks \r\n\t\t\t\t Conservation Easements \r\n\t\t\t\t Conservation Funds \r\n\t\t\t\t Pathways for People and Nature \r\n\t\t\t\t Pollinator Pathways \r\n\t\t\t\t Rain Barrel Community Program 2026 \r\n\t\t\t\t Town Ordinances & Resolutions \r\n\t\t\t\t Trail Maps \r\n\t\t\t\t Turtlefest \r\n\t\t\t\t Useful Resources \r\n\t\t\t\t Wetlands \r\n\t\t\t\t Economic Development \r\n\t\t\t\t Energy & Environment Advisory Committee \r\n\t\t\t\t Visit our Facebook Page \r\n\t\t\t\t Highway Safety Committee \r\n\t\t\t\t Licensing Board \r\n\t\t\t\t Long-Range Planning Subcommittee \r\n\t\t\t\t Ordinance Oversight Committee \r\n\t\t\t